Package: infometrics
Type: Package
Title: Information-Theoretic Methods for Econometric Estimation
Version: 0.2.0
Date: 2026-05-17
Authors@R: person("Author", "Name",
    email = "author@example.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements the class of Information-Theoretic (IT) estimators
    for econometric models, following the unified framework of Golan (2008).
    Provides entropy measures (Shannon, Kullback-Leibler, Renyi, Tsallis,
    Cressie-Read) and the classical Maximum Entropy (ME) and Cross-Entropy
    (CE) estimators in both primal (constrained) and dual (concentrated)
    form. The dual concentrated formulation is used by default for
    computational efficiency. Inference tools include normalized entropy,
    entropy-ratio statistics, and pseudo-R-squared measures. Also provides
    the Generalized Maximum Entropy (GME) and Generalized Cross-Entropy (GCE)
    regression estimators via a single gme() function.
